{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>YHWH alone did guide him</b>. HaShem will cause Israel to dwell securely alone, and there is none with Him — this is an epithet for HaShem or for Israel. The meaning is that Israel has no prince or ruler from among the sons of Elohim who guides it or assists in its guidance, but HaShem alone, for He is its portion and inheritance, as He mentioned, and I have already written this (Leviticus 18:25). And in the Sifrei (Ha'azinu 12): \"YHWH alone did guide him\" — the Holy One, blessed be He, said to them: just as you dwelt alone in this world and derived no benefit from any of the nations, so am I destined to settle you alone in the time to come, and not one of the nations will derive benefit from you at all. \"And there is no strange El with Him\" — that no authority be given to any of the princes of the nations of the world to come and exercise dominion over you, as it is said: \"And I am going out, and behold, the prince of Greece is coming\" (Daniel 10:20), and \"the prince of the kingdom of Persia is standing before me\" (ibid. v. 13), \"but I will tell you what is inscribed in the writing of truth...\" (ibid. v. 21)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {0 "Ramban's citation of Leviticus 18:25 likely refers to his comment there on the nations' appointed heavenly princes; the verse reference appears correct."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:15:45.390804421Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}